## 4. Dataset Description

We use the ZZU pediatric ECG dataset [REF: Tan2025_ZZU], which is, at the time of writing, the largest openly available pediatric ECG corpus with explicit cardiovascular disease diagnoses. The dataset was acquired at the First Affiliated Hospital of Zhengzhou University between January 2018 and May 2024, under IRB approval that waived informed consent for de-identified scientific reuse.

**Cohort.** 11,643 hospitalised children, ages 0–14 (6,740 male, 4,903 female; age unit recorded in days). The age distribution is heavily skewed toward older children, with 4,000+ recordings in the 12–14 year range and a long tail toward the neonatal end (Fig. 1 of [REF: Tan2025_ZZU]).

**Recordings.** 14,190 total ECG records. 12,334 are full 12-lead (I, II, III, aVR, aVL, aVF, V1–V6); 1,856 are 9-lead, with V2/V4/V6 substituted by V1/V3/V5 — a deliberate concession to lead-placement difficulty in young children [REF: Tan2025_ZZU]. Sampling rate 500 Hz; record length 5–120 s, with ~93% in the 20–40 s range.

**Labels.** ECG diagnostic statements are encoded under both the AHA/ACC/HRS standard [REF: Kligfield2007] and a Chinese expert consensus standard [REF: Guo2019]. Disease diagnoses are ICD-10–coded [REF: WHO_ICD10]. Of the 14,190 records, 3,716 carry one or more cardiovascular disease labels; 10,474 carry other disease labels but no cardiac diagnosis.

**Quality control.** Three signal-quality indices — pSQI (high-frequency noise), basSQI (baseline wander), bSQI (beat-detection agreement) — are reported per lead in the released metadata [REF: Tan2025_ZZU].

**Disease grouping used here.** The 19 cardiovascular disease categories in the ZZU dataset span myocarditis, cardiomyopathy, Kawasaki disease, and a range of congenital heart defects (Table 2 of [REF: Tan2025_ZZU]). For modelling we collapse these into three broader categories that align with clinical decision-making at triage time:

| Class | Composition | Records (approx.) |
|---|---|---|
| 0 — Normal / Non-cardiac | No cardiovascular ICD-10 label | {PLACEHOLDER: N} |
| 1 — Structural Heart Disease | Congenital defects (VSD, ASD, ToF, PDA, PS), cardiomyopathy | {PLACEHOLDER: N} |
| 2 — Arrhythmia & Electrical | Myocarditis with conduction disturbance, Kawasaki with cardiac involvement, other arrhythmic labels | {PLACEHOLDER: N} |

We chose this three-class framing because (a) per-disease cell counts in the 19-class breakdown are too small for robust per-fold patient-disjoint evaluation, and (b) the three groups correspond to clinically distinct downstream pathways. We acknowledge in Section 15 that this grouping discards within-class heterogeneity that future work could recover.

