## 10. Evaluation Metrics

We report macro-F1 (primary), accuracy, macro-AUROC (one-vs-rest), and per-class F1. Macro-F1 is primary because the class distribution is imbalanced — the Normal/Non-cardiac class dominates — and macro-F1 weights all classes equally. AUROC complements F1 by being threshold-free.

Statistical comparison between fusion and the strongest single expert is done by paired comparison across the five fold-level F1 scores; we report mean, std, and a paired-sample 95% CI on the difference. With n = 5 folds, formal significance testing is underpowered; we report the CI honestly rather than claim statistical significance.

For interpretability we report (i) IG–GradCAM Pearson r per class, (ii) IG–occlusion top-20% region overlap and Pearson r per class.

